"""Every sound effect of 88fits regenerated by an AI sound model (pass 60): Stable Audio first, AudioGen as the alternate.

Garry (2026-10-08): "I don't quite like how high pitched everything is ... go over the sound effects that we have in the
game and regenerate them ... Remove all the voice effects, including hit sounds, all that voice stuff." Later the same
day: "for audio, I switched from using AudioCraft to now using Stable Audio 3, which is sitting on this URL -
http://127.0.0.1:7861/". So: one prompt per sound id in a lower, duller register, three candidates each per engine,
post-processed and scored (a lower spectral centroid wins), the best bound in the sound map as `real/<id>.wav`; the ten
Kokoro voice lines are replaced by non-voice sounds (same ids) or silenced (pl_hurt, pl_jump -> real/silence.wav). The
six mu_* music rows are never touched.

Engines (`--engine`, default stable):
- stable: Garry's Stable Audio app (Gradio 6.3.0 at STABLE_URL; `gradio_client` 2.x speaks its SSE protocol), endpoint
  `/generate`: prompt, negative prompt, seconds_total, cfg, steps, seed, ping-pong sampler. Its defaults (8 steps,
  cfg 1.0) are the distilled model's own sampling: about 1.5 s for a 2 s clip, 44.1 kHz stereo, exactly the asked length.
  The prompt gets STABLE_SUFFIX ("Sound effect, no music, no voice.") because this model honours such words.
- audiogen: audiocraft_plus (Gradio 3.50.2, queue on, at AUDIOGEN_HOST), AudioGen medium = dependency AUDIOGEN_FN with
  49 inputs; gradio_client 2.x refuses its websocket protocol, so this speaks the Gradio 3.50 queue protocol itself over
  websocket-client. 16 kHz mono, no negative prompting (the bare description only), about 9 s for a 3 s clip. The 345
  candidates of the first run (pass 60, before the switch) are the alternates on the listening page.

Run (from the repo root; python 3.10 with gradio_client, websocket-client, numpy, scipy, soundfile, librosa):
  python tools/ai_sfx.py                           # generate every missing Stable candidate, score, pick, write real/, bind
  python tools/ai_sfx.py --gen-only                # only generate (resume-safe: existing candidates are skipped)
  python tools/ai_sfx.py --only pk_gem_s,pk_coin --force       # these ids again
  python tools/ai_sfx.py --only w_snake_bite --cands 6         # three more candidates (c3..c5) for a hard id, picked with the rest
  python tools/ai_sfx.py --dry-run                 # print the table and what would be generated
  python tools/ai_sfx.py --pick pk_gem_s=1         # pick Stable candidate 1 by ear (kept over --auto), write it, bind it
  python tools/ai_sfx.py --pick pk_gem_s=audiogen:2            # keep the AudioGen alternate instead
  python tools/ai_sfx.py --auto                    # pick every id by score (manual picks kept unless --force)
  python tools/ai_sfx.py --rescore && python tools/ai_sfx.py --auto   # after a change to the scoring rules: scores again from the stored measures, picks again
  python tools/ai_sfx.py --bind                    # write real/ + the soundmap rows from the picks, no generation
  python tools/ai_sfx.py --report                  # old vs new centroid and level per id, the engines' share
  python tools/ai_sfx.py --docs                    # docs/design/src/sounds.json (the bible's section 16) from the table
  python tools/ai_sfx.py --engine audiogen --gen-only          # the alternate engine (same flags)
Then, under the Godot lock: godot --headless --path game --import ; godot ... --script res://tools/import_json.gd -- only=sounds

Files: tools/dl/sfx60/<engine>/<id>_c<k>.wav (+ .json: prompt, seed, duration, steps, cfg) are the raw candidates as the
server gave them, tools/dl/sfx60/<engine>/proc/<id>_c<k>.wav the processed ones (what the review page plays),
tools/dl/sfx60/<engine>/scores.json every candidate's numbers, tools/dl/sfx60/picks.json the chosen engine + candidate
per id, generate_stable.log / generate.log the run logs. game/content/sounds/real/<id>.wav is the picked sound at
22.05 kHz 16-bit mono, content RMS -14 dBFS with the peaks limited at -2 dBFS (TARGET_RMS_DB, CEILING_DB).
"""
